from pathlib import Path
import json,posixpath
ROOT=Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1];BASE=ROOT/'Class 9'/'English Medium'/'Physical Education'
for d in ('Chapters','Concepts','Definitions','Exercises'):(BASE/d).mkdir(parents=True,exist_ok=True)
chapters=[
('Food-Health-Happiness','7-23','The chapter connects well-being with balanced nutrition, regular physical activity, emotional health and social relationships. A story about a young athlete introduces persistence and achievement; a cricket biography shows how sustained effort supports performance. Illustrated activities include games, dance and calorie-intake/activity tables. Learners compare energy from foods with energy used during activities, consider lifestyle risks and disease prevention, and reflect on healthy routines. The textbook presents a BMI calculation and chart as a classroom learning tool.'),
('Achieve Fitness, Preserve Posture','24-39','Fitness involves health-related capacities and performance-related components such as agility, balance, coordination, power, speed and reaction time. Game activities let learners practise these skills. The chapter introduces yoga postures and benefits, then examines posture and deformities including kyphosis, with symptoms, possible causes, prevention and corrective exercise guidance. Illustrations support posture checks and movement sequences; the exercises encourage observing safe form and regular practice.'),
('The Safety Ring of Care','40-47','The chapter develops prevention and first-response awareness for water-related accidents, drowning and choking. It emphasizes avoiding unsafe water entry, calling for help, and following safe first-aid steps illustrated in the book. Swimming is presented for fitness, recreation and life-saving capability. Classroom games reinforce communication and safety decisions. The content distinguishes prevention, rescue and first aid, and stresses adult/emergency assistance.'),
('Active Society','48-56','Participation in sport can support physical development, coordination, teamwork, leadership, discipline, inclusion and social well-being. The chapter defines sport culture through values and everyday practices and invites learners to identify barriers to participation. Cooperative games such as First the Leader, Circle of Friends, Captain Ball and Move as One teach shared rules, turn-taking, coordination and inclusive leadership. Activities ask students to plan improvements to participation in school and community.'),
('Knowing Nature through Games','57-66','Outdoor and adventure activities connect physical education with place, landscape and environmental awareness. The chapter introduces trekking, water sports, kayaking, paragliding, mountain biking, ice skating and beach sports through illustrated examples and short descriptions. Learners compare activities, identify equipment and safety considerations, and observe local natural features. The closing tasks ask students to design nature-friendly games and reflect on responsible participation.'),
('Annexure — Lifestyle Formation','67-84','The annexure turns health learning into a daily routine: nutritious food, regular movement, appropriate screen habits, study/rest balance and sleep. It illustrates warm-up movements before activity and cool-down stretches afterward, with step-by-step photographs. The sequence includes upper-body, trunk and lower-body stretches, walking/jogging and relaxation. Follow the activity book’s teacher guidance and adjust movement to safe individual ability.')]
concepts=[
('Health, Fitness and Well-being','Food-Health-Happiness','7-15','Health includes physical, mental and social well-being. The chapter connects healthy habits, nutrition, activity, social support and emotional qualities with a satisfying life. Fitness is developed through regular participation, not a single performance.'),
('Energy Balance and Food Choice','Food-Health-Happiness','14-19','Food supplies energy and nutrients; physical activity uses energy. The illustrated tables compare selected food calories with activity expenditure. A sustained mismatch can contribute to unhealthy weight change. The text encourages varied food, regular activity and reflection on lifestyle patterns rather than judging health from one meal.'),
('BMI as a Screening Measure','Food-Health-Happiness','21-23','The activity book defines Body Mass Index as body mass in kilograms divided by height in metres squared: BMI = mass(kg)/height(m)². It includes a reference chart for classroom interpretation. BMI is a screening indicator in this lesson; it is not a complete diagnosis of an individual’s health.'),
('Health-Related and Performance-Related Fitness','Achieve Fitness, Preserve Posture','25-29','The chapter distinguishes fitness capacities associated with health from those supporting sport performance. It names agility (changing direction), balance (maintaining stability), coordination (combining movements), power (forceful movement), speed and reaction time. Games provide practice contexts.'),
('Posture and Kyphosis','Achieve Fitness, Preserve Posture','33-39','Posture is body alignment while standing, sitting or moving. The text discusses kyphosis, its visible curvature, possible causes and signs such as back discomfort, and describes preventive habits and exercises. Correct movement, ergonomic habits and adult guidance support safe practice.'),
('Water Safety and First Aid','The Safety Ring of Care','40-47','Prevention comes first: avoid entering unsafe water, use appropriate supervision and seek trained help. The book’s drowning-response sequence emphasizes checking safety, calling emergency help, supporting the person from a safe position, and following first-aid/CPR guidance only when trained. Choking content likewise separates prevention from prompt first aid and emergency response.'),
('Sport Culture, Inclusion and Socialisation','Active Society','48-56','Sport culture comprises the values, customs and practices around participation, spectatorship and play. Inclusive sport adapts participation so different abilities and backgrounds can take part. Shared games build belonging, leadership, cooperation and respect when rules are fair and roles rotate.'),
('Nature-Based and Adventure Activities','Knowing Nature through Games','57-66','The chapter surveys land, water, air and snow activities, relating each to terrain and equipment. Trekking, kayaking, paragliding, mountain biking, ice skating and beach sports involve distinct environmental and safety requirements. Nature-friendly participation respects ecosystems and local conditions.'),
('Warm-up and Cool-down','Annexure — Lifestyle Formation','71-84','Warm-up prepares the body for activity and helps transition into more vigorous movement. Cool-down follows activity, allowing a gradual return toward rest. The illustrated sequences show controlled stretches, walking/jogging and relaxation; movements should be performed smoothly without forcing painful ranges.')]
definitions=[
('Body Mass Index','Food-Health-Happiness','22','A ratio relating body mass to squared height: BMI = mass in kilograms ÷ (height in metres)². The activity book provides a chart for classroom discussion.'),
('Agility, Balance and Coordination','Achieve Fitness, Preserve Posture','26','Agility is the ability to change direction quickly; balance is the ability to maintain control of body position; coordination is the ability to combine body movements smoothly.'),
('Kyphosis','Achieve Fitness, Preserve Posture','35-38','A postural deformity involving an excessive outward curve of the upper back. The activity book illustrates posture, symptoms and prevention/remedial exercise examples.'),
('Sport Culture','Active Society','49','The shared values, customs and practices associated with sport, including participation, spectatorship and social interaction.'),
]
exercises=[
('Food-Health-Happiness — Reflection and Activities','Food-Health-Happiness','8-23','Activities examine persistence and achievement, explore food and activity calories, compare daily habits, and reflect on physical, emotional and social components of health. The book includes tables and a BMI activity; use these as learning prompts, not diagnoses.'),
('Achieve Fitness — Games, Yoga and Posture','Achieve Fitness, Preserve Posture','25-39','Games practise agility, balance, coordination, power, speed and reaction time. Yoga/posture tasks use illustrated steps, observation and reflection. Learners identify kyphosis prevention and safe movement habits; follow teacher guidance and do not force painful positions.'),
('Safety Ring — Prevention and Response','The Safety Ring of Care','41-47','Review the book’s prevention advice, identify safe responses to drowning/choking situations and distinguish calling for help, rescue and trained first aid. Swimming and safety games reinforce discussion. Use adult/emergency support in real incidents.'),
('Active Society — Inclusive Games','Active Society','49-56','Practise the chapter games by following the stated rules, rotating roles and ensuring every learner can participate. Reflect on leadership, teamwork, inclusion and the social benefits of sport.'),
('Knowing Nature — Outdoor Activity Projects','Knowing Nature through Games','58-66','Compare outdoor/adventure activities, identify terrain and equipment, discuss safety and environmental care, and design a locally suitable nature-friendly game.'),
('Lifestyle Formation — Daily Routine and Stretching','Annexure — Lifestyle Formation','68-84','Use the illustrated daily routine and warm-up/cool-down sequences to plan balanced activity, sleep and study. Practise stretches under teacher supervision, with controlled movement and individual adaptation.')]
def write(folder,name,kind,chapter,pages,body,rels=()):
 p=BASE/folder/(name+'.md');tag=kind.lower();links='\n'.join(f'- [[{posixpath.relpath(r,folder)}]]' for r in rels) or '- [[../Subject Overview]]'
 p.write_text(f'''---\nclass: 9\nmedium: English\nsubject: Physical Education\nchapter: "{chapter}"\ntopic: "{name}"\ntype: {tag}\ntextbook: Health and Physical Education Standard IX Activity Book\nprinted_pages: "{pages}"\ntags: [class/9, medium/english, subject/physical-education, type/{tag}]\n---\n# {name}\n\n{body}\n\n**Textbook reference:** Health and Physical Education Standard IX Activity Book, printed pp. {pages}.\n\n## Related notes\n{links}\n''',encoding='utf-8');return p
nodes=[('Subject Overview.md',5)]; chapter_ids={}; lookup={}
for i,(title,pages,body) in enumerate(chapters,1):
 n=f'Chapter {i:02d} - {title}'; chapter_ids[title]=f'n{i+1}'; write('Chapters',n,'chapter',title,pages,body,[f'Concepts/{x[0]}' for x in concepts if x[1]==title]+[f'Definitions/{x[0]}' for x in definitions if x[1]==title]+[f'Exercises/{x[0]}' for x in exercises if x[1]==title]);nodes.append((f'Chapters/{n}.md',5))
for folder,data,color,kind in [('Concepts',concepts,1,'concept'),('Definitions',definitions,2,'definition'),('Exercises',exercises,4,'exercise')]:
 for title,chapter,pages,body in data:
  write(folder,title,kind,chapter,pages,body,[f'Chapters/Chapter {i:02d} - {chapter}' for i,(t,_,_) in enumerate(chapters,1) if t==chapter]);nodes.append((f'{folder}/{title}.md',color))
overview='''---\nclass: 9\nmedium: English\nsubject: Physical Education\nedition: First Edition 2024\ntype: overview\ntags: [class/9, medium/english, subject/physical-education, type/overview]\n---\n# Health & Physical Education — Standard IX\n\n**Activity Book, First Edition 2024.** All 88 PDF pages were visually reviewed, including game rules, nutrition tables, posture diagrams, safety guidance, sports illustrations, the lifestyle annexure, warm-up/cool-down movements and closing inserts.\n\n## Chapters\n'''+''.join(f'- [[Chapters/Chapter {i:02d} - {t}|{t}]] — printed pp. {p}\n' for i,(t,p,_) in enumerate(chapters,1))+'''\n## Colour legend\n- Red `#FF6B6B`: key concepts\n- Orange `#F4A261`: definitions\n- Yellow `#E9C46A`: health rules and measures\n- Green `#2A9D8F`: activities and examples\n- Blue `#457B9D`: chapters and overview\n- Purple `#9B5DE5`: cross-chapter connections\n\nOpen [[Physical Education.canvas]] for the activity map.\n'''
(BASE/'Subject Overview.md').write_text(overview,encoding='utf-8')
allnodes=[('Subject Overview.md',5)]+nodes[1:];cn=[]
for i,(file,col) in enumerate(allnodes):cn.append({'id':f'n{i+1}','type':'file','file':file,'x':(i%3)*500,'y':(i//3)*180,'width':360,'height':130,'color':str(col)})
edges=[]
for i in range(6):edges.append({'id':f'e{i+1}','fromNode':'n1','fromSide':'right','toNode':f'n{i+2}','toSide':'left','color':'5'})
lookup={n['file']:n['id'] for n in cn}
for folder,data in [('Concepts',concepts),('Definitions',definitions),('Exercises',exercises)]:
 for x in data:
  title,chapter,_,_=x;source=chapter_ids[chapter];target=lookup[f'{folder}/{title}.md'];edges.append({'id':f'e{len(edges)+1}','fromNode':source,'fromSide':'right','toNode':target,'toSide':'left','color':'5'})
for a,b in [('Energy Balance and Food Choice','BMI as a Screening Measure'),('Health-Related and Performance-Related Fitness','Posture and Kyphosis'),('Water Safety and First Aid','Nature-Based and Adventure Activities'),('Sport Culture, Inclusion and Socialisation','Nature-Based and Adventure Activities'),('Warm-up and Cool-down','Health-Related and Performance-Related Fitness')]:edges.append({'id':f'e{len(edges)+1}','fromNode':lookup[f'Concepts/{a}.md'],'fromSide':'right','toNode':lookup[f'Concepts/{b}.md'],'toSide':'left','color':'6'})
(BASE/'Physical Education.canvas').write_text(json.dumps({'nodes':cn,'edges':edges},indent=2),encoding='utf-8')
